& [BoundaryFormation] separates parsing from acquisition and admission
  + [inside] one exact caller-supplied successful byte region and explicit resource limits
  + [inside] checked scalar decoding, chain traversal, strict UTF-16, exact stream-name grammar, and all-or-fault release
  + [outside] making the Win32 call, owning a handle, dereferencing a pointer, proving API success, completeness, same-handle origin, filesystem support, or freshness
  + [outside] named-stream admission, entry observation, traversal, Git reconciliation, topology receipt, mutation, seal, and promotion
  + [correction_only] authority lineage changes while profile semantics and production behavior remain unchanged

& [AtomicRequirementSet] is complete
  + [M2B-SIP-001] bind strict profile, exact region, explicit limits, source snapshot, and governing correction source
  + [M2B-SIP-002] decode the fixed 24-byte little-endian header without pointer casts
  + [M2B-SIP-003] require every nonterminal offset to progress, fit, and align to eight bytes
  + [M2B-SIP-004] require positive even name-byte lengths within the caller UTF-16-unit bound
  + [M2B-SIP-005] decode strict UTF-16LE without replacement or NUL termination
  + [M2B-SIP-006] admit exactly the default DATA name or a nonempty named DATA stream grammar
  + [M2B-SIP-007] reject negative signed stream and allocation sizes before unsigned release
  + [M2B-SIP-008] require the terminal record to exhaust the exact supplied region
  + [M2B-SIP-009] preserve source order and source offsets while ignoring uninterpreted alignment padding
  + [M2B-SIP-010] preserve closed faults, bounded allocation, no partial release, proof, rollback, and nonclaims
  + [M2B-SIP-011] preserve zero dependency, zero unsafe, and zero runtime-effect boundaries
  + [M2B-SIP-012] supersede the prior non-governing signature without erasing it
  + [M2B-SIP-013] revalidate the unchanged implementation and evidence under the governing replacement signature

& [DataDesignModel] is one bounded parser
  + [ParseLimits] is maximum entries 1 through 1024 and maximum name UTF-16 units 1 through 32767
  + [RawStreamRecord] is exact decoded name, stream size u64, allocation size u64, and source byte offset u32
  + [ParseFault] is one closed limit, header, offset, alignment, length, size, UTF-16, name, terminal, or resource code with bounded detail
  + [lifecycle] is exact bytes to per-record validation to complete vector or one fault
  + [state] is local parser variables only
  + [provenance] is byte-region structure and caller-supplied syntax only
  - never: return records accumulated before a later fault

& [ChainAlgorithm] is checked
  + [step_1] validate limits and minimum nonempty region
  + [step_2] enforce entry budget before each header
  + [step_3] require 24 header bytes and decode little-endian fields from slices
  + [step_4] validate positive even bounded name-byte length
  + [step_5] establish current entry boundary from terminal region end or checked nonterminal next offset
  + [step_6] require name end within current entry boundary
  + [step_7] decode strict UTF-16LE and exact DATA-stream wrapper grammar
  + [step_8] reject negative sizes and preserve exact nonnegative values
  + [step_9] preserve source order and source byte offset
  + [step_10] advance exactly by nonterminal offset or require terminal exact exhaustion and release once

& [ConstraintLedger] is fail closed
  + [C-01] original and correction sources remain byte-bound and separate from derived artifacts
  + [C-02] profile remains cantor-windows-stream-info-parser/0.1
  + [C-03] production code and behavior remain unchanged during authority correction
  + [C-04] arithmetic is checked and offset progress is exact
  + [C-05] nonterminal offsets are eight-byte aligned and remain inside the region
  + [C-06] names are positive, even, bounded, and strict UTF-16LE
  + [C-07] grammar is exactly ::$DATA or :nonempty:$DATA
  + [C-08] signed sizes reject before u64 conversion
  + [C-09] terminal exhaustion is exact and padding is ignored only inside a nonterminal record boundary
  + [C-10] partial records never release
  + [C-11] Cargo, lockfile, dependency, pointer, unsafe, and effect deltas are zero
  + [C-12] physical completeness, provenance, and stream-admission claims are absent
  + [C-13] old authority is preserved as superseded, not rewritten

& [SubcomponentWeaveTrace] is source grounded
  + [header] originates in ChainIntent and weaves to little-endian fixture tests
  + [offset] originates in alignment and terminal intent and weaves to progress, alignment, bounds, and exhaustion tests
  + [name] originates in ChainIntent and weaves to length, strict UTF-16, and grammar tests
  + [sizes] originate in ChainIntent and weave to negative-value rejection tests
  + [padding] originates in ChainIntent and weaves to nonzero-padding acceptance tests
  + [authority] originates in ObservedFault and weaves to canonical supersession and binding evidence

& [CrossWeaveTrace] joins existing fabric
  + [unsafe_seam_research] supplies the future byte-copy boundary but receives no implementation authority
  + [entry_policy] is a sibling prerequisite and does not interpret stream records
  + [supplied_observation_assembly] may consume parser outputs only after corrected authority revalidation and applies separate uniqueness and admission rules
